// expect-error: T223
// Z3 corpus #48: axis-1 — Wall 4 Step 6 T223 positional-with-refinement.
//
// WHAT THIS FIXTURE PROVES
//
// N4-S6 / T223 sub-case 1: a refinement `where` clause is admitted
// ONLY on a fully-named variant payload. The variant below uses the
// positional form `Positive(i64)` (no field name) but declares
// `where x > 0`. The parser rejects with T223 at variant-declaration
// time — BEFORE any type-check or Z3 work happens.
//
// Per A1-S6 the T223 registry hint covers all four sub-cases at a
// generic level (positional-with-refinement, mixed payload, duplicate
// field name, zero-payload-with-refinement).
//
// THE LANGUAGE PRIMITIVES THIS NEEDED
//
//   * Step 6 parser's named/positional disambiguation (N17-S6).
//   * Step 6 parser's where-clause precondition check on payload form.
//   * T223 diagnostic code.
//
// MUTATION CONTRACT
//
// Adding `x:` before the type (`Positive(x: i64) where x > 0`) flips
// this fixture to the expect-ok side and drops T223. The fixture
// remains a parse error otherwise.
module sigil;

enum SignedInt {
    Positive(i64) where x > 0,  // MUTATION_SITE
    Zero,
}

entry actor Main {
    on Tick() -> i64 {
        return 1;
    }
}
